<title>Dictionary Analysis</title>
<context ID_DICTIONARY_ANALYSIS IDD_DICTIONARY_ANALYSIS />

While editing or viewing a data dictionary, you can generate several reports that analyze the contents of the dictionary. To access these reports, select <b>Dictionary Analysis</b> from the <b>View</b> menu. A dialog box will appear with the following reports:


<subheader>Items</subheader>

<b>Items with mismatched DecChar options</b>: Lists numeric items that have a <link decimal_character.csdoc>decimal character</link> option that differs from the dictionary's default option. You generally want every item in a dictionary to use the same option.

<b>Items with mismatched ZeroFill options</b>: Lists numeric items that have a <link zero_fill.csdoc>zero fill</link> option that differs from the dictionary's default option. You generally want every item in a dictionary to use the same option.


<subheader>Value Sets</subheader>

<b>Items without value sets</b>: Lists items that do not have a value set.

<b>Numeric items without value sets</b>: Lists numeric items that do not have a value set. Without a value set, users can enter unexpected data (such as -5 for a two-digit age field), so it is a good idea to define a value set for all numeric items.

<b>Numeric items with overlapping value sets</b>: Lists numeric value sets that have discrete or range values that overlap.


<seealso dictionary_macros.csdoc />
